# Web styling: MUI

The web app styles with Material UI only. `docs/ui.md` is the design-system reference, and the runtime theme in `apps/web/src/lib/theme/` is the source of every token.

- Style with the `sx` prop and theme tokens (`"primary.main"`, `"text.secondary"`, `"divider"`), so light and dark modes both work.
- Use responsive objects for breakpoints: `sx={{ p: { xs: 2, sm: 3, lg: 4 } }}`.
- Build layout from `Box`, `Stack`, `Container`, `Paper variant="outlined"` and `Typography`; show loading with `Skeleton`.
- Check a change with `pnpm web check:design-system`.

The Android app (`apps/mobile`) uses React Native components, not MUI.
